# Interactive tmux debug runtime tests

- [ ] Real tmux is exercised with a fake Devin process; no model call occurs.
- [ ] The fake role output is visible through capture-pane before process exit.
- [ ] A running pane cannot be sealed.
- [ ] Every graceful-exit key is recorded and forces development-only evidence.
- [ ] Final output, DONE and export survive process exit and bundle sealing.
- [ ] Launch receipt proves task text was not shell-interpolated.
- [ ] A sandboxed spec is not silently accepted by the no-sandbox debug profile.
- [ ] Explicit abort kills only the private tmux server, preserves the live bundle, and seals an `ABORTED` receipt.
